findings.explanation:
Step 1 and addendum 3 ask for the following, measured before and after the fixes:
- milestone times;
- kills per minute in manual combat and slimes within 30 studs on arrival;
- taps per kill for each class;
- Lv5 -> iron weapon time and daily N-kill minutes;
- 60 s+ stretches where the next action was unclear.
Only a raw attribute log exists, and Lv5 was never reached. In run 2 (Horns), TutorialKills hit 5 at t=155.6 s, but TutorialStep stayed 2 (unclaimed) for the rest of the log. That is roughly 9 minutes across two Play restarts; the cause is unknown (intentional or claim hard to find). The bot created at 14:05 fires Swing at exactly SwingInterval and moves the character with Humanoid:MoveTo. Its kills/min is an upper bound, and RELEASE_PLAN forbids reporting bot hunting as a new-player result.

Several changes were made that are not in the prompt or A23:
- in non-PvP zones, taking damage no longer cancels Travel;
- the player's own nametag is hidden;
- the interact key changed from G to E (skill is now Q only);
- shop prompts open on a tap (HoldDuration 0);
- a slime wobble motion layer was added in Fx.
They are probably from the user's playtest feedback, but no doc records them. Their comments cite a '2026-10-06 playtest' on 2026-10-05, which will mislead later readers about when they were tested.

Still open:
- the skill button shows no MP cost (client-ui-07);
- the shop panel stays 'pending' after a server rejection (shop-7);
- an active kaiju can still trade at the anvil (no KaijuState check in ShopService);
- trades made through the HUD/U-key panel do not set BlacksmithVisited (shop-6);
- personal-slime leftovers remain in Config.Tutorial;
- all 39 'blocked upload' comments are unchanged;
- existing completers still get the pinned '무기 살펴보기' row.
